text:
To turn this mock-up into a colorful website, you can use HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Here's a brief outline of the steps to create the website:

1. Create a new HTML file and add a `<div>` container to hold the jokes.
```html
<div id="joke-container">
  <div class="joke-1">
    <h2>Joke 1</h2>
    <p>I'm not a morning person.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="joke-2">
    <h2>Joke 2</h2>
    <p>Why did the tomato turn red?</p>
  </div>
</div>
```
1. Add a CSS file to style the jokes and the overall website.
```css
#joke-container {
  margin: 0 auto;
  max-width: 500px;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  border-radius: 5px;
}

.joke-1,
.joke-2 {
  margin-bottom: 20px;
}

.joke-1 h2 {
  color: #333;
  font-size: 24px;
}

.joke-1 p {
  color: #666;
  font-size: 18px;
}

.joke-2 h2 {
  color: #666;
  font-size: 24px;
}

.joke-2 p {
  color: #333;
  font-size: 18px;
}
```
1. Add a JavaScript file to handle the joke-swapping functionality.
